//? Title: U-Net cropped skips and learned decoding
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Pixel classification needs fine boundaries as well as broad spatial context. U-Net combines a contracting CNN with learned decoding and aligned encoder skips; this report checks crops and gradients before a visible compact Adam fit and held-out mask evaluation.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/unet.cpp`.

> The method

Encoder pooling increases context while learned transposed convolutions restore spatial resolution. Concatenated,cropped skip features preserve detail for each decoder pair. Original valid geometry and compact SAME geometry remain explicit and separately checked.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/unet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/unet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/unet_concept.tikz > build/unet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/unet_concept.svg build/unet_concept.dvi > build/unet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
